Consider the following intermediate program segment in three address code:
$$
\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{u}=\mathrm{v} ~* ~\mathrm{w} \\
& \mathrm{w}=\mathrm{u}~+~\mathrm{w} \\
& \mathrm{x}=\mathrm{u}~/~ \mathrm{w} \\
& \mathrm{v}=\mathrm{u}~-~\mathrm{x}
\end{aligned}
$$
The minimum number of total variables required to convert the above code segment to static single assignment form is ?

What is the value of the attribute E.val after parsing the expression " $4 / 2 / 2$ " using the following translation scheme?
$$
\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{E} \rightarrow \mathrm{~T} / \mathrm{E}_{1}\{\text { E.val }=\mathrm{T} . \mathrm{val} / \mathrm{E} 1 . \mathrm{val}\} \\\\
& \mathrm{E} \rightarrow \mathrm{~T}\{\text { E.val }=\mathrm{T} . \mathrm{val}\} \\\\
& \mathrm{T} \rightarrow \text { digit }\{\mathrm{T} . \mathrm{val}=\text { val}(\text {digit})\}
\end{aligned}
$$
